The benchmark tasks are adapted from BigCodeBench, by the BigCode project
(https://huggingface.co/datasets/bigcode/bigcodebench), which is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. Each task was rewritten from one BigCodeBench task, named in its record's
`source.seed_id`: a language model turned it into a request for one Python function, with its
own test inputs and reference solutions, and the expected outputs come from running those
solutions. Every task was then checked automatically and reviewed by hand.

This software and data are provided "AS IS", without warranties or conditions of any kind (see
sections 7 and 8 of the licence). The evaluation harness installs the third-party packages that
responses import and runs model-written code, so run it on a machine or in a container you are
willing to lose.
